# Builder.io Fusion rules — Agency Workspace

Internal tool for a study-abroad agency: an Admin sees all students and staff;
Staff see only their assigned students. Handles personal student data and
documents, so the boundaries below are hard requirements, not preferences.

`AGENTS.md` in this repo is the full version of these rules. Read it too.

## Fusion draws. Code decides.

Build **presentational UI**. Data access, auth, and permissions are
hand-written and out of scope for generated code.

## Never create, edit, or delete these

- `src/lib/supabase/**` — database and auth clients
- `src/proxy.ts` — session handling and route protection
- `supabase/**` — schema migrations and Row Level Security policies
- `**/actions.ts` and `src/app/api/**` — Server Actions and route handlers
- `scripts/**` and `.github/**` — CI guardrails
- any route under a `superadmin` path

If a request seems to need one of these, say so and stop. Do not work around it.

## Never do this

- Do not write Supabase queries, or import from `@supabase/supabase-js`,
  `@supabase/ssr`, or `@/lib/supabase/**`. **Use the mock fixtures in
  `@/lib/mock/students.ts`.**
- Do not reference `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`. It bypasses all row-level
  security and must never appear in application or component code.
- Do not add authorization logic to a component. Do not treat a hidden column,
  row, or nav link as access control — the database enforces that.
- Do not add a link to any superadmin route. It is intentionally unlisted.
- Do not add another UI or component library, and do not add the Builder SDK
  (`@builder.io/*`) as a runtime dependency — this app renders its own UI.
- Do not hard-code status strings. Import them from `@/types/db` and render the
  `*_STATUS_LABELS` values. The status values are still **placeholders** pending
  the owner's confirmation.

## Always do this

- Follow the worked example: `src/app/(admin)/admin/students/page.tsx` plus
  `src/components/students/students-table.tsx`.
- Pages are `async` Server Components that fetch and pass typed props down.
  Components take props and render — not `async`, no data fetching.
- Compose the existing shadcn/ui primitives in `src/components/ui/**`
  (Tailwind v4, base-nova style, neutral base, lucide icons).
- Type everything against `@/types/db`. No `any`.
- Import via the `@/*` alias.
- Give every list an empty state, and every awaiting route a `loading.tsx`.
- Format dates with an explicit locale and `timeZone: "UTC"` to avoid
  hydration mismatches.

## Environment

Run with `NEXT_PUBLIC_UI_PREVIEW=true` — screens render from mock fixtures with
no Supabase project and no login. **No other environment variables are needed,
and no real credentials should ever be added to this project's environment.**
